From 258d05a7e6f4df1d958fcc6b8c565fa9aef76570 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:53:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 208/211] i18n: translate Gatekeeper + Wireless strings (24
 langs); tokenize 14 menu labels

Full language pass over the menus and Reaper pages found two gaps beyond the
known Gatekeeper one:

- 55 Gatekeeper (RGK_*) strings were English-seeded in all 24 non-EN dicts.
- 57 Wireless-diagnostics (RWIF_*) strings were likewise English-seeded.
- 14 menu / tab labels were hardcoded English in menuTrees/menuTree.js
  (AI Advisor, System Info/Sysinfo, VPN Status, VPN Director, DNS Director,
  Tweaks, Site Survey, Traffic Limiter, NFS Exports, Temperature,
  Notification, Security Update Notification).

Fix:
- menuTree.js: the 14 labels tokenized. 5 reuse existing ASUS/Reaper keys
  (Reaper_c_ai_advisor, Reaper_c_system_info, fan_tuning_temperature,
  Notification_security_update, WiFi_sitesurvey); 7 new Reaper_c_* keys minted
  (traffic_limiter, nfs_exports, dns_director, vpn_status, vpn_director,
  notification, tweaks) and appended (English) to all 25 dicts. Acronym/brand
  labels (IPv6, VPN, SNMP, WDS, MLO, AiMesh, Free WiFi...) left raw, matching
  ASUS's own menu convention.
- All 112 RGK_*/RWIF_* + 7 new keys machine-translated into the 24 non-EN
  languages (native review still owed, per the v1.6.0 policy). Values spliced
  by line index preserving 25-dict key-order lockstep; brand/technical terms
  (Gatekeeper, Reaper, MAC, Wi-Fi, SSID, DSCP, VPN, DNS, NFS, GHz...) kept in
  English where the translator judged so.
- Removed a stray BOM-only temp.dict (untracked build-tool residue).

Validated: 25-dict lockstep (5786 lines each), JS-context quote/backslash lint
clean on every RGK_*/RWIF_* value in all 25 dicts (they sit in JS string
literals on Reaper_GK.asp / Reaper_Wireless.asp), every referenced menu token
resolves in all 25 dicts. Known limit: the Gatekeeper captive 'awaiting
approval' page is C-generated in httpd (outside the dict pipeline) and stays
English.

Dicts-and-menu only, no code-path change. All 5 models inherit at next bump.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
